{"id":"eels","title":"turbo_eels.x","program":"turbo_eels.x","package":"turboEELS","version":"7.5","html":"<section class=\"qe-section qe-sec-intro\" id=\"intro\" data-kind=\"intro\" data-title=\"Introduction\"><h2 class=\"qe-section-title\">Introduction</h2>\n\n<div class=\"qe-indent\"><p class=\"qe-flow\">Input data format: { } = optional, [ ] = it depends.</p>\n<p class=\"qe-flow\">All quantities whose dimensions are not explicitly specified are in<br>RYDBERG ATOMIC UNITS</p>\n<p class=\"qe-flow\">BEWARE: TABS, DOS &lt;CR&gt;&lt;LF&gt; CHARACTERS ARE POTENTIAL SOURCES OF TROUBLE</p>\n<p class=\"qe-flow\">Comment lines in namelists can be introduced by a \"!\", exactly as in\nfortran code. Comments lines in ``cards'' can be introduced by\neither a \"!\" or a \"#\" character in the first position of a line.</p>\n<pre class=\"qe-pre\"><b>Structure of the input data:</b>\n===============================================================================\n\n&amp;LR_INPUT\n  ...\n/\n\n&amp;LR_CONTROL\n  ...\n/</pre></div>\n</section>\n   <section class=\"qe-section qe-sec-namelist\" id=\"LR_INPUT\" data-kind=\"namelist\" data-title=\"&amp;LR_INPUT\" data-name=\"LR_INPUT\"><h2 class=\"qe-section-title\"><span class=\"qe-kind\">Namelist</span> <span class=\"qe-nl\">&amp;LR_INPUT</span></h2><div class=\"qe-layout\">\n      <p><b> This namelist is always needed !\n      </b></p>\n      <article class=\"qe-var\" id=\"prefix\" data-var=\"prefix\"><header class=\"qe-var-head\"><h3 class=\"qe-var-name\"><a class=\"qe-self\" href=\"#prefix\">prefix</a></h3> <span class=\"qe-type\" title=\"Fortran type\">CHARACTER</span> <span class=\"qe-var-tools\" data-var=\"prefix\"></span></header><dl class=\"qe-meta\"><div class=\"qe-meta-row qe-meta-default\"><dt>Default</dt><dd>'pwscf'</dd></div></dl><div class=\"qe-desc\"><p class=\"qe-flow\">Sets the prefix for generated and read files. The files\ngenerated by the ground state pw.x run must have this\nsame prefix.</p></div></article>\n\n      <article class=\"qe-var\" id=\"outdir\" data-var=\"outdir\"><header class=\"qe-var-head\"><h3 class=\"qe-var-name\"><a class=\"qe-self\" href=\"#outdir\">outdir</a></h3> <span class=\"qe-type\" title=\"Fortran type\">CHARACTER</span> <span class=\"qe-var-tools\" data-var=\"outdir\"></span></header><dl class=\"qe-meta\"><div class=\"qe-meta-row qe-meta-default\"><dt>Default</dt><dd>'./'</dd></div></dl><div class=\"qe-desc\"><p class=\"qe-flow\">The directory that contains the run critical files, which\ninclude the files generated by ground state pw.x run.</p></div></article>\n\n      <article class=\"qe-var\" id=\"restart\" data-var=\"restart\"><header class=\"qe-var-head\"><h3 class=\"qe-var-name\"><a class=\"qe-self\" href=\"#restart\">restart</a></h3> <span class=\"qe-type\" title=\"Fortran type\">LOGICAL</span> <span class=\"qe-var-tools\" data-var=\"restart\"></span></header><dl class=\"qe-meta\"><div class=\"qe-meta-row qe-meta-default\"><dt>Default</dt><dd>.false.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"qe-desc\"><p class=\"qe-flow\">When set to .true., turbo_eels.x will attempt to restart\nfrom a previous interrupted calculation. (see <a href=\"#restart_step\" data-local=\"restart_step\">restart_step</a>\nvariable).\nBeware, if set to .false. turbo_eels.x will OVERWRITE any\nprevious runs.</p></div></article>\n\n      <article class=\"qe-var\" id=\"restart_step\" data-var=\"restart_step\"><header class=\"qe-var-head\"><h3 class=\"qe-var-name\"><a class=\"qe-self\" href=\"#restart_step\">restart_step</a></h3> <span class=\"qe-type\" title=\"Fortran type\">INTEGER</span> <span class=\"qe-var-tools\" data-var=\"restart_step\"></span></header><dl class=\"qe-meta\"><div class=\"qe-meta-row qe-meta-default\"><dt>Default</dt><dd>itermax</dd></div></dl><div class=\"qe-desc\"><p class=\"qe-flow\">The code writes restart files every restart_step iterations.\nRestart files are automatically written at the end of\nitermax Lanczos steps.</p></div></article>\n\n      <article class=\"qe-var\" id=\"lr_verbosity\" data-var=\"lr_verbosity\"><header class=\"qe-var-head\"><h3 class=\"qe-var-name\"><a class=\"qe-self\" href=\"#lr_verbosity\">lr_verbosity</a></h3> <span class=\"qe-type\" title=\"Fortran type\">INTEGER</span> <span class=\"qe-var-tools\" data-var=\"lr_verbosity\"></span></header><dl class=\"qe-meta\"><div class=\"qe-meta-row qe-meta-default\"><dt>Default</dt><dd>1</dd></div></dl><div class=\"qe-desc\"><p class=\"qe-flow\">This integer variable controls the amount of information\nwritten to standard output.</p></div></article>\n\n      <article class=\"qe-var\" id=\"disk_io\" data-var=\"disk_io\"><header class=\"qe-var-head\"><h3 class=\"qe-var-name\"><a class=\"qe-self\" href=\"#disk_io\">disk_io</a></h3> <span class=\"qe-type\" title=\"Fortran type\">CHARACTER</span> <span class=\"qe-var-tools\" data-var=\"disk_io\"></span></header><dl class=\"qe-meta\"><div class=\"qe-meta-row qe-meta-default\"><dt>Default</dt><dd>'default'</dd></div></dl><div class=\"qe-desc\"><pre class=\"qe-pre\">    Fine control of disk usage. Currently only 'reduced' is\nsupported where no restart files are written, apart from\nthe 'default' mode.</pre></div></article>\n\n   </div></section>\n   <section class=\"qe-section qe-sec-namelist\" id=\"LR_CONTROL\" data-kind=\"namelist\" data-title=\"&amp;LR_CONTROL\" data-name=\"LR_CONTROL\"><h2 class=\"qe-section-title\"><span class=\"qe-kind\">Namelist</span> <span class=\"qe-nl\">&amp;LR_CONTROL</span></h2><div class=\"qe-layout\">\n      <article class=\"qe-var\" id=\"approximation\" data-var=\"approximation\"><header class=\"qe-var-head\"><h3 class=\"qe-var-name\"><a class=\"qe-self\" href=\"#approximation\">approximation</a></h3> <span class=\"qe-type\" title=\"Fortran type\">CHARACTER</span> <span class=\"qe-var-tools\" data-var=\"approximation\"></span></header><dl class=\"qe-meta\"><div class=\"qe-meta-row qe-meta-default\"><dt>Default</dt><dd>'TDDFT'</dd></div></dl><div class=\"qe-desc\">\n<p class=\"qe-flow\">A string describing a level of theory:</p>\n<dl class=\"qe-options\"><div class=\"qe-opt\"><dt><code>'TDDFT'</code></dt><dd><p class=\"qe-flow\">Time-Dependent Local Density Approximation or<br>Time-Dependent Generalized Gradient Approximation\n(depending on the XC functional)</p></dd></div><div class=\"qe-opt\"><dt><code>'IPA'</code></dt><dd><p class=\"qe-flow\">Independent Particle Approximation (IPA)</p></dd></div><div class=\"qe-opt\"><dt><code>'RPA_with_CLFE'</code></dt><dd><p class=\"qe-flow\">Random Phase Approximation (RPA) with<br>Crystal Local Field Effects (CLFE)</p></dd></div></dl>\n\n</div></article>\n\n      <article class=\"qe-var\" id=\"q1\" data-var=\"q1\"><header class=\"qe-var-head\"><h3 class=\"qe-var-name\"><a class=\"qe-self\" href=\"#q1\">q1, q2, q3</a></h3> <span class=\"qe-type\" title=\"Fortran type\">REAL</span> <span class=\"qe-var-tools\" data-var=\"q1\"></span></header><dl class=\"qe-meta\"><div class=\"qe-meta-row qe-meta-default\"><dt>Default</dt><dd>1.0, 1.0, 1.0</dd></div></dl><div class=\"qe-desc\"><p class=\"qe-flow\">The values of the transferred momentum q = (q1, q2, q3)\nin Cartesian coordinates in units of 2pi/a, where\n\"a\" is the lattice parameter.</p></div></article>\n\n      <article class=\"qe-var\" id=\"calculator\" data-var=\"calculator\"><header class=\"qe-var-head\"><h3 class=\"qe-var-name\"><a class=\"qe-self\" href=\"#calculator\">calculator</a></h3> <span class=\"qe-type\" title=\"Fortran type\">CHARACTER</span> <span class=\"qe-var-tools\" data-var=\"calculator\"></span></header><dl class=\"qe-meta\"><div class=\"qe-meta-row qe-meta-default\"><dt>Default</dt><dd>'lanczos'</dd></div></dl><div class=\"qe-desc\">\n<p class=\"qe-flow\">Variable that controls which algorithm is used to compute EELS spectra.</p>\n<dl class=\"qe-options\"><div class=\"qe-opt\"><dt><code>'lanczos'</code></dt><dd><p class=\"qe-flow\">corresponds to the Lanczos recursive algorithm</p></dd></div><div class=\"qe-opt\"><dt><code>'sternheimer'</code></dt><dd><p class=\"qe-flow\">corresponds to the Sternheimer algorithm</p></dd></div></dl>\n\n</div></article>\n\n      <article class=\"qe-var\" id=\"itermax\" data-var=\"itermax\"><header class=\"qe-var-head\"><h3 class=\"qe-var-name\"><a class=\"qe-self\" href=\"#itermax\">itermax</a></h3> <span class=\"qe-type\" title=\"Fortran type\">INTEGER</span> <span class=\"qe-var-tools\" data-var=\"itermax\"></span></header><dl class=\"qe-meta\"><div class=\"qe-meta-row qe-meta-default\"><dt>Default</dt><dd>500</dd></div></dl><div class=\"qe-desc\"><p class=\"qe-flow\">When <a href=\"#calculator\" data-local=\"calculator\">calculator</a> = 'lanczos', <a href=\"#itermax\" data-local=\"itermax\">itermax</a> is the\nmaximum number of Lanczos iterations that will be performed.\nWhen <a href=\"#calculator\" data-local=\"calculator\">calculator</a> = 'sternheimer', <a href=\"#itermax\" data-local=\"itermax\">itermax</a> is the\nmaximum number of iterations in a SCF step for each frequency.</p></div></article>\n\n      <article class=\"qe-var\" id=\"pseudo_hermitian\" data-var=\"pseudo_hermitian\"><header class=\"qe-var-head\"><h3 class=\"qe-var-name\"><a class=\"qe-self\" href=\"#pseudo_hermitian\">pseudo_hermitian</a></h3> <span class=\"qe-type\" title=\"Fortran type\">LOGICAL</span> <span class=\"qe-var-tools\" data-var=\"pseudo_hermitian\"></span></header><dl class=\"qe-meta\"><div class=\"qe-meta-row qe-meta-default\"><dt>Default</dt><dd>.true.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"qe-desc\"><p class=\"qe-flow\">This variable is used only when <a href=\"#calculator\" data-local=\"calculator\">calculator</a> = 'lanczos'.\nWhen set to .true. the pseudo-Hermitian Lanczos algorithm is\nused. When set to .false. the non-Hermitian Lanczos\nbiorthogonalization algorithm is used (which is two times slower).</p></div></article>\n\n      <article class=\"qe-var\" id=\"alpha_mix\" data-var=\"alpha_mix\"><header class=\"qe-var-head\"><h3 class=\"qe-var-name\"><a class=\"qe-self\" href=\"#alpha_mix\">alpha_mix(i)</a></h3> <span class=\"qe-type\" title=\"Fortran type\">REAL</span> <span class=\"qe-var-tools\" data-var=\"alpha_mix\"></span></header><dl class=\"qe-meta\"><div class=\"qe-meta-row qe-meta-default\"><dt>Default</dt><dd>alpha_mix(1)=0.7</dd></div></dl><div class=\"qe-desc\"><p class=\"qe-flow\">This variable is used only when <a href=\"#calculator\" data-local=\"calculator\">calculator</a> = 'sternheimer'.\nMixing parameter (for the i-th iteration) for updating\nthe response SCF potential using the modified Broyden\nmethod: D.D. Johnson, <a href=\"https://journals.aps.org/prb/abstract/10.1103/PhysRevB.38.12807\" class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">PRB 38, 12807 (1988)</a>.</p></div></article>\n\n      <article class=\"qe-var\" id=\"epsil\" data-var=\"epsil\"><header class=\"qe-var-head\"><h3 class=\"qe-var-name\"><a class=\"qe-self\" href=\"#epsil\">epsil</a></h3> <span class=\"qe-type\" title=\"Fortran type\">REAL</span> <span class=\"qe-var-tools\" data-var=\"epsil\"></span></header><dl class=\"qe-meta\"><div class=\"qe-meta-row qe-meta-default\"><dt>Default</dt><dd>0.02</dd></div></dl><div class=\"qe-desc\"><p class=\"qe-flow\">This variable is used only when <a href=\"#calculator\" data-local=\"calculator\">calculator</a> = 'sternheimer'.\nThe broadening/damping term (in Rydberg units).</p></div></article>\n\n      <article class=\"qe-var\" id=\"units\" data-var=\"units\"><header class=\"qe-var-head\"><h3 class=\"qe-var-name\"><a class=\"qe-self\" href=\"#units\">units</a></h3> <span class=\"qe-type\" title=\"Fortran type\">INTEGER</span> <span class=\"qe-var-tools\" data-var=\"units\"></span></header><dl class=\"qe-meta\"><div class=\"qe-meta-row qe-meta-default\"><dt>Default</dt><dd>0</dd></div></dl><div class=\"qe-desc\"><pre class=\"qe-pre\">This variable is used only when <a href=\"#calculator\" data-local=\"calculator\">calculator</a> = 'sternheimer'.\nThe unit system used for the output, for <a href=\"#start\" data-local=\"start\">start</a>, <a href=\"#end\" data-local=\"end\">end</a>,\nand <a href=\"#increment\" data-local=\"increment\">increment</a> input parameters.\n0 = Rydbergs, 1 = Electron volts.</pre></div></article>\n\n      <article class=\"qe-var\" id=\"start\" data-var=\"start\"><header class=\"qe-var-head\"><h3 class=\"qe-var-name\"><a class=\"qe-self\" href=\"#start\">start</a></h3> <span class=\"qe-type\" title=\"Fortran type\">REAL</span> <span class=\"qe-var-tools\" data-var=\"start\"></span></header><dl class=\"qe-meta\"><div class=\"qe-meta-row qe-meta-default\"><dt>Default</dt><dd>0.0</dd></div><div class=\"qe-meta-row qe-meta-see\"><dt>See</dt><dd><a href=\"#end\" data-local=\"end\">end</a>, <a href=\"#increment\" data-local=\"increment\">increment</a></dd></div></dl><div class=\"qe-desc\"><p class=\"qe-flow\">This variable is used only when <a href=\"#calculator\" data-local=\"calculator\">calculator</a> = 'sternheimer'.\n<a href=\"#start\" data-local=\"start\">start</a> is the value of frequency starting from which the\nsusceptibility and the loss function (-Im(1/eps)) will be computed.\n<a href=\"#start\" data-local=\"start\">start</a> is specified in units controlled by <a href=\"#units\" data-local=\"units\">units</a>.</p></div></article>\n\n      <article class=\"qe-var\" id=\"end\" data-var=\"end\"><header class=\"qe-var-head\"><h3 class=\"qe-var-name\"><a class=\"qe-self\" href=\"#end\">end</a></h3> <span class=\"qe-type\" title=\"Fortran type\">REAL</span> <span class=\"qe-var-tools\" data-var=\"end\"></span></header><dl class=\"qe-meta\"><div class=\"qe-meta-row qe-meta-default\"><dt>Default</dt><dd>2.5</dd></div><div class=\"qe-meta-row qe-meta-see\"><dt>See</dt><dd><a href=\"#start\" data-local=\"start\">start</a>, <a href=\"#increment\" data-local=\"increment\">increment</a></dd></div></dl><div class=\"qe-desc\"><p class=\"qe-flow\">This variable is used only when <a href=\"#calculator\" data-local=\"calculator\">calculator</a> = 'sternheimer'.\n<a href=\"#end\" data-local=\"end\">end</a> is the value of frequency up to which the\nsusceptibility and the loss function (-Im(1/eps)) will be computed.\n<a href=\"#end\" data-local=\"end\">end</a> is specified in units controlled by <a href=\"#units\" data-local=\"units\">units</a>.</p></div></article>\n\n      <article class=\"qe-var\" id=\"increment\" data-var=\"increment\"><header class=\"qe-var-head\"><h3 class=\"qe-var-name\"><a class=\"qe-self\" href=\"#increment\">increment</a></h3> <span class=\"qe-type\" title=\"Fortran type\">REAL</span> <span class=\"qe-var-tools\" data-var=\"increment\"></span></header><dl class=\"qe-meta\"><div class=\"qe-meta-row qe-meta-default\"><dt>Default</dt><dd>0.001</dd></div><div class=\"qe-meta-row qe-meta-see\"><dt>See</dt><dd><a href=\"#start\" data-local=\"start\">start</a>, <a href=\"#end\" data-local=\"end\">end</a></dd></div></dl><div class=\"qe-desc\"><p class=\"qe-flow\">This variable is used only when <a href=\"#calculator\" data-local=\"calculator\">calculator</a> = 'sternheimer'.\n<a href=\"#increment\" data-local=\"increment\">increment</a> is an incremental step used to define the mesh\nof frequencies between <a href=\"#start\" data-local=\"start\">start</a> and <a href=\"#end\" data-local=\"end\">end</a>.\n<a href=\"#increment\" data-local=\"increment\">increment</a> is specified in units controlled by <a href=\"#units\" data-local=\"units\">units</a>.</p></div></article>\n\n      <article class=\"qe-var\" id=\"ethr_nscf\" data-var=\"ethr_nscf\"><header class=\"qe-var-head\"><h3 class=\"qe-var-name\"><a class=\"qe-self\" href=\"#ethr_nscf\">ethr_nscf</a></h3> <span class=\"qe-type\" title=\"Fortran type\">REAL</span> <span class=\"qe-var-tools\" data-var=\"ethr_nscf\"></span></header><dl class=\"qe-meta\"><div class=\"qe-meta-row qe-meta-default\"><dt>Default</dt><dd>1.D-11</dd></div></dl><div class=\"qe-desc\"><p class=\"qe-flow\">Threshold for the convergence of eigenvalues during\nthe iterative diagonalization of the Hamiltonian in\nthe non-self-consistent-field (NSCF) calculation at\nk and k+q points. Note, this quantity is NOT extensive.</p></div></article>\n\n   </div></section>","sections":[{"id":"intro","title":"Introduction","kind":"intro","level":0,"varIds":[]},{"id":"LR_INPUT","title":"&LR_INPUT","kind":"namelist","name":"LR_INPUT","level":0,"varIds":["prefix","outdir","restart","restart_step","lr_verbosity","disk_io"]},{"id":"LR_CONTROL","title":"&LR_CONTROL","kind":"namelist","name":"LR_CONTROL","level":0,"varIds":["approximation","q1","calculator","itermax","pseudo_hermitian","alpha_mix","epsil","units","start","end","increment","ethr_nscf"]}],"variables":[{"id":"prefix","names":["prefix"],"display":"prefix","type":"CHARACTER","default":"'pwscf'","sectionId":"LR_INPUT","sectionTitle":"&LR_INPUT","options":[],"summary":"Sets the prefix for generated and read files."},{"id":"outdir","names":["outdir"],"display":"outdir","type":"CHARACTER","default":"'./'","sectionId":"LR_INPUT","sectionTitle":"&LR_INPUT","options":[],"summary":"The directory that contains the run critical files, which include the files generated by ground state pw.x run."},{"id":"restart","names":["restart"],"display":"restart","type":"LOGICAL","default":".false.","sectionId":"LR_INPUT","sectionTitle":"&LR_INPUT","options":[],"summary":"When set to .true., turbo_eels.x will attempt to restart from a previous interrupted calculation."},{"id":"restart_step","names":["restart_step"],"display":"restart_step","type":"INTEGER","default":"itermax","sectionId":"LR_INPUT","sectionTitle":"&LR_INPUT","options":[],"summary":"The code writes restart files every restart_step iterations."},{"id":"lr_verbosity","names":["lr_verbosity"],"display":"lr_verbosity","type":"INTEGER","default":"1","sectionId":"LR_INPUT","sectionTitle":"&LR_INPUT","options":[],"summary":"This integer variable controls the amount of information written to standard output."},{"id":"disk_io","names":["disk_io"],"display":"disk_io","type":"CHARACTER","default":"'default'","sectionId":"LR_INPUT","sectionTitle":"&LR_INPUT","options":[],"summary":"Fine control of disk usage."},{"id":"approximation","names":["approximation"],"display":"approximation","type":"CHARACTER","default":"'TDDFT'","sectionId":"LR_CONTROL","sectionTitle":"&LR_CONTROL","options":["'TDDFT'","'IPA'","'RPA_with_CLFE'"],"summary":"A string describing a level of theory: 'TDDFT' Time-Dependent Local Density Approximation or Time-Dependent Generalized Gradient Approximation (depending on the XC functional) 'IPA' Independent Particle Approximation…"},{"id":"q1","names":["q1","q2","q3"],"display":"q1, q2, q3","type":"REAL","default":"1.0, 1.0, 1.0","sectionId":"LR_CONTROL","sectionTitle":"&LR_CONTROL","options":[],"summary":"The values of the transferred momentum q = (q1, q2, q3) in Cartesian coordinates in units of 2pi/a, where \"a\" is the lattice parameter."},{"id":"calculator","names":["calculator"],"display":"calculator","type":"CHARACTER","default":"'lanczos'","sectionId":"LR_CONTROL","sectionTitle":"&LR_CONTROL","options":["'lanczos'","'sternheimer'"],"summary":"Variable that controls which algorithm is used to compute EELS spectra. 'lanczos' corresponds to the Lanczos recursive algorithm 'sternheimer' corresponds to the Sternheimer algorithm"},{"id":"itermax","names":["itermax"],"display":"itermax","type":"INTEGER","default":"500","sectionId":"LR_CONTROL","sectionTitle":"&LR_CONTROL","options":[],"summary":"When calculator = 'lanczos', itermax is the maximum number of Lanczos iterations that will be performed."},{"id":"pseudo_hermitian","names":["pseudo_hermitian"],"display":"pseudo_hermitian","type":"LOGICAL","default":".true.","sectionId":"LR_CONTROL","sectionTitle":"&LR_CONTROL","options":[],"summary":"This variable is used only when calculator = 'lanczos'."},{"id":"alpha_mix","names":["alpha_mix"],"display":"alpha_mix(i)","type":"REAL","default":"alpha_mix(1)=0.7","sectionId":"LR_CONTROL","sectionTitle":"&LR_CONTROL","options":[],"summary":"This variable is used only when calculator = 'sternheimer'."},{"id":"epsil","names":["epsil"],"display":"epsil","type":"REAL","default":"0.02","sectionId":"LR_CONTROL","sectionTitle":"&LR_CONTROL","options":[],"summary":"This variable is used only when calculator = 'sternheimer'."},{"id":"units","names":["units"],"display":"units","type":"INTEGER","default":"0","sectionId":"LR_CONTROL","sectionTitle":"&LR_CONTROL","options":[],"summary":"This variable is used only when calculator = 'sternheimer'."},{"id":"start","names":["start"],"display":"start","type":"REAL","default":"0.0","sectionId":"LR_CONTROL","sectionTitle":"&LR_CONTROL","options":[],"summary":"This variable is used only when calculator = 'sternheimer'. start is the value of frequency starting from which the susceptibility and the loss function (-Im(1/eps)) will be computed. start is specified in units…"},{"id":"end","names":["end"],"display":"end","type":"REAL","default":"2.5","sectionId":"LR_CONTROL","sectionTitle":"&LR_CONTROL","options":[],"summary":"This variable is used only when calculator = 'sternheimer'. end is the value of frequency up to which the susceptibility and the loss function (-Im(1/eps)) will be computed. end is specified in units controlled by units."},{"id":"increment","names":["increment"],"display":"increment","type":"REAL","default":"0.001","sectionId":"LR_CONTROL","sectionTitle":"&LR_CONTROL","options":[],"summary":"This variable is used only when calculator = 'sternheimer'. increment is an incremental step used to define the mesh of frequencies between start and end. increment is specified in units controlled by units."},{"id":"ethr_nscf","names":["ethr_nscf"],"display":"ethr_nscf","type":"REAL","default":"1.D-11","sectionId":"LR_CONTROL","sectionTitle":"&LR_CONTROL","options":[],"summary":"Threshold for the convergence of eigenvalues during the iterative diagonalization of the Hamiltonian in the non-self-consistent-field (NSCF) calculation at k and k+q points."}],"aliases":{"id3":"prefix","prefix":"prefix","id4":"outdir","outdir":"outdir","id5":"restart","restart":"restart","id6":"restart_step","restart_step":"restart_step","id7":"lr_verbosity","lr_verbosity":"lr_verbosity","id8":"disk_io","disk_io":"disk_io","id10":"approximation","approximation":"approximation","id11":"q1","q1":"q1","id12":"q1","q2":"q1","id13":"q1","q3":"q1","id14":"calculator","calculator":"calculator","id15":"itermax","itermax":"itermax","id16":"pseudo_hermitian","pseudo_hermitian":"pseudo_hermitian","id17":"alpha_mix","alpha_mix":"alpha_mix","id18":"epsil","epsil":"epsil","id19":"units","units":"units","id20":"start","start":"start","id21":"end","end":"end","id22":"increment","increment":"increment","id23":"ethr_nscf","ethr_nscf":"ethr_nscf","id9":"LR_CONTROL","LR_CONTROL":"LR_CONTROL","id2":"LR_INPUT","LR_INPUT":"LR_INPUT","id1":"intro"}}